platformd-trustd NEWS
=====================

CHANGES WITH 0.1.5:

        * Session lock state and verification freshness are now independent.
          Session creation and unlock events do not establish freshness.
          Freshness is recorded only from a qualifying successful
          platformd-verify event and is invalidated before suspend.

        * SubmitAuthEvent now validates field types and lengths, the declared
          user name and user ID, the logind session, and session ownership.
          Ordinary PAM session records remain audit evidence but do not
          establish verification freshness.

        * Session records now expose the lock state, verification timestamp,
          source, and evidence quality separately. Authentication event records
          include their session ID and whether they qualified for freshness.

        * Policy results now include stable machine-readable reason codes.
          Unknown session class, activity, lock, or verification state fails
          closed instead of being treated as satisfied.

platformd-trustd 0.1.4

  * The service unit grants read/write access to systemd's char-tpm device
    group under DevicePolicy=closed, so the default service configuration can
    use the TPM without exposing unrelated physical devices.
  * The local-trusted-session policy now denies remote sessions and sessions
    whose locality cannot be determined. Verification freshness uses
    CLOCK_BOOTTIME and is invalidated before suspend.
  * Runtime measurement failures mark the log incomplete. GetRuntimeLog
    exposes this through a new complete field, and attestation-token production
    fails unless the runtime NV value is readable and certified by the same
    attestation key used for the boot quote.
  * TPM TCTI and ESYS contexts have explicit ownership and are released on all
    initialization and failure paths.
  * Boot references are stored per kernel-install entry. trustctl provision
    accepts a reference identifier, trustctl remove-boot-reference removes one
    entry, and the kernel-install plugin updates and removes entries
    independently. The legacy single-reference file remains readable.
  * UKI reference provisioning and PCR reporting build cleanly with GCC 16
    release-mode truncation diagnostics enabled.

platformd-trustd 0.1.3

  Audit hardening:

  * Evidence-producing Varlink methods (Attest, GetAttestationToken,
    GetEnrollment, ActivateCredential) are now restricted to root. Producing a
    TPM quote or certification is a signing operation on a shared, slow device;
    reading recorded state stays open to every local peer.
  * The TCG event log is read to EOF rather than truncated at 64 KiB. A
    truncated log cannot be replayed, so a short read now returns no log instead
    of incomplete evidence.
  * A session that already existed when the daemon started is recorded with its
    freshness unknown ("never verified"), not fresh-as-of-now, so a daemon
    restart no longer resets every session's freshness clock. Sessions observed
    being created still start fresh (their creation is a successful auth).
  * pam_platformd.so: the account-phase gate returns PAM_PERM_DENIED (the
    account-phase idiom) rather than PAM_AUTH_ERR; the client accepts either a
    runtime directory ($PLATFORMD_TRUSTD_RUNTIME) or a socket path
    ($PLATFORMD_TRUST_SOCKET).

platformd-trustd 0.1.2

  * pam_platformd.so gains a gate role: with a policy= argument on an auth or
    account line it evaluates a trust policy and passes or fails (fail closed), so
    a PAM stack can offer strong factors only on a verified boot. A verified-boot
    policy is added to EvaluatePolicy. Reference stack in
    pam/platformd-gate.example; documented in pam_platformd(8).

platformd-trustd 0.1.1

  * The kernel-install plugin is installed where kernel-install scans
    (/usr/lib/kernel/install.d, derived from systemd's prefix), so the boot
    reference is provisioned on each UKI update.

platformd-trustd 0.1.0

  * Full RATS Attester and local Verifier: verified-local boot graded against a
    kernel-install-provisioned reference; in-process verification of
    systemd-homed identities (Ed25519); an extend-only NV runtime auth log; a TPM
    quote and an IETF Entity Attestation Token (RFC 9711) bundling boot and
    runtime evidence; attestation-key enrollment by EK credential activation; and
    the fresh-user-verification and local-trusted-session policies.

platformd-trustd 0.0.1

  * Observability core: boot identity and logind sessions as read-only records
    over the Varlink interface io.platformd.Trust; trustctl status /
    list-sessions / session.
